        </hspi:project>
        <hspi:dates>
            <hspi:plannedAcquisitionTime>
                <hspi:startDate>2026-04-01</hspi:startDate>
                <hspi:endDate>2026-09-30</hspi:endDate>
            </hspi:plannedAcquisitionTime>
            <hspi:deliveryDate>120 days from completion of data acquisition.</hspi:deliveryDate>
        </hspi:dates>
        <hspi:purpose>The project area is spread throughout Lake Erie, with most of the surveys located in central Lake Erie, and with additional surveys in the approaches to Buffalo and in Lake Ontario. Lake Erie borders multiple large US and Canadian cities and supports several major ports and local communities. Most of the project area has not been surveyed since the 1940s. Lake Erie is highly trafficked by commercial and recreational vessels. There are several ferry routes that connect small islands with the mainland within the western project extents. The western portion of the lake is one of the most shallow in all of the Great Lakes, making danger to navigation identification critical. This project will contribute to the collaborative Lakebed 2030 initiative to map the Great Lakes. A significant portion of the survey is located within the proposed Lake Erie National Marine Sanctuary. Surveying this area will help inform the designation of this sanctuary. Additional surveys will be conducted within the Lake Ontario National Marine Sanctuary. Mapping will help identify critical habitats located within the sanctuaries.</hspi:purpose>
