        <hspi:shorelineAndFeature>
            <hspi:instructions>Feature investigation assignments and related information are provided in the GIS files extended attribute schema in the project instruction package.

The potentially assigned features in the following object classes only require visual verification, unless otherwise specified in the aforementioned extended attributes:
LNDARE, LNDMRK, MORFAC (CATMOR = 1, dolphin), PILPNT, and SBDARE (NATSUR = rock, ledge).  If one of the above features is not seen, contact PM before conducting a feature disproval.</hspi:instructions>
        </hspi:shorelineAndFeature>
        <hspi:physicalSeabedSamples assigned="true">
            <hspi:instructions>Identify 5-7 bottom sample locations per survey sheet in geological areas of interest as observed in the acquired backscatter imagery and/or in areas of potential vessel anchoring. Bottom sample locations shall be spaced at least 2400 meters apart. Do NOT plan to acquire bottom samples where the water depth is greater than 80 meters or within dredged channels (DRGARE), pipeline and cable areas (PIPSOL, CBLARE), or fairways and approaches to a channel (FAIRWY).</hspi:instructions>
        </hspi:physicalSeabedSamples>
        <hspi:reporting assigned="true">
            <hspi:instructions>Adhere to all progress reporting, survey reports, and survey findings requirements.  NOAA field units must use Scribble for reporting survey progress.</hspi:instructions>
        </hspi:reporting>
        <hspi:HPPOC>
            <hspi:instructions>Field units shall not release any information regarding the location of any specific potentially historic and/ or culturally significant anthropogenic features encountered during data collection (e.g., coordinates, depth, etc.) to the public, nor shall the information be included in the Report of Survey. The one exception to this requirement is when the feature poses an immediate danger to navigation. If a feature poses an immediate danger to navigation, the field shall send the information required for charting to the Marine Chart Division for immediate application to the chart per NOS Hydrographic Specifications and deliverables.</hspi:instructions>
        </hspi:HPPOC>
        <hspi:affectedENC assigned="true">
            <hspi:instructions>The ENC suite is actively undergoing rescheming and subject to change. Ensure the latest editions of the largest scale ENCs are used for all data investigations and comparisons.</hspi:instructions>
        </hspi:affectedENC>
